---
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout
  title="To Rise Supplies case study — Evelyn R."
  description="A ChatGPT prompt template I wrote and shared with my team to draft content for around 40 new products a week."
>

  <article class="case-study">
    <a href="/#work" class="case-back-float" aria-label="Back to work">←</a>
    <a href="/#work" class="case-back"><span class="arrow">←</span> Back to work</a>

    <p class="eyebrow scroll-reveal">Case study — To Rise Supplies</p>
    <h1 class="scroll-reveal" style="--reveal-delay: 0.06s">A ChatGPT prompt template for product content</h1>
    <p class="case-meta scroll-reveal" style="--reveal-delay: 0.12s">Web &amp; Content Operations Developer · Dec 2022 – Sept 2023 · ChatGPT</p>
    <a href="https://www.torisesupplies.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="case-live scroll-reveal" style="--reveal-delay: 0.18s">Visit the website <span class="arrow arrow-out">↗</span></a>

    <div class="case-body">
      <h2 class="scroll-reveal">The problem</h2>
      <p class="scroll-reveal">
        To Rise Supplies is a B2B distributor of restaurant and food-service supplies. We added around 40 new products a week. For each one, we searched other sites for a similar product by its title and dimensions, and used that as a base to write our own content.
      </p>

      <h2 class="scroll-reveal">What I did</h2>
      <p class="scroll-reveal">
        When ChatGPT was still new, I wrote a prompt template: you add the product's title and dimensions, and it returns a first draft of the product content. We always reviewed and edited each draft before publishing. I shared it with my teammates who did the same work, and they started using it too.
      </p>

      <h2 class="scroll-reveal">Result</h2>
      <p class="scroll-reveal">
        Each new product started from a ready draft instead of research from zero.
      </p>
    </div>

    <a href="/#contact" class="case-cta scroll-reveal">Work with me →</a>
  </article>

</MainLayout>
